    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="1020" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg924"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your No. 6 received. The President does not understand that our commissioners in
                    Cuba have undertaken such discussion as you mention. But as a measure of
                    precaution he has instructed them not to admit or discuss question of
                    relinquishment of title or sovereignty and to restrict themselves to the
                    military operation of evacuation. You are right in understanding that questions
                    of relinquishment of title and sovereignty are committed to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
